The '''Narquois''' were a short-sized [[species]] that [[Homeworld|hailed]] from the [[planet]] of [[Narq]]. Their skin, their [[eye]]s, and the filaments that grew from their heads were all [[Color|blue]], as a means of camouflage in the [[fungus]] [[forest]]s of their homeworld. One notable Narquois was [[Pru Sweevant]], a bandit who attacked vulnerable convoys thanks to his contacts within the [[Mining Guild]].

==Biology and appearance==
The Narquois were [[Sentience|sentient]] [[humanoid]]s that had evolved from [[tree]]-dwelling [[Narquois precursor species|animals]]. The [[Color|blue]] coloration of their skin as well as the [[hair]]-like filaments that grew from their heads served as camouflage in the [[fungus]] [[forest]]s of their [[homeworld]]. Their hands featured five digits, including an opposable thumb, each sporting a hard nail. Members of the species were diminutive,<ref name="Aliens of the Galaxy" /> as exemplified by the [[pirate]] [[Pru Sweevant]].<ref name="TFAVD" />

==Society and culture==
The Narquois were capable thinkers and skilled [[technician]]s.<ref name="Aliens of the Galaxy" /> Some of them knew [[Galactic Basic Standard]].<ref name="Aftermath">[[Aftermath (novel)|''Aftermath'']]</ref>

==History==
[[File:NeimoidiansSWE.png|thumb|left|150px|The Narquois were slaves to their greedy Neimoidian neighbors for centuries.]]
The Narquois were the sentient descendants of an arboreal, [[Narquois precursor species|non-sentient species]]. They evolved on [[Narq]], a wet and gloomy planet situated in the [[Colonies]] region of [[the galaxy]]. Hundreds of [[Standard year|years]] before the [[Cold War]], they found themselves at the mercy of the [[Neimoidian]]s, a greedy civilization from neighboring [[Neimoidia]] who were building up an empire of wealthy "[[Purse world|purse-worlds]]" for themselves. The Neimoidians occupied Narq and started treating its natives as virtual [[Slavery|serfs]]. Although the Narquois were quite clever, their new masters denied their intelligence, forcing them to work only as [[Mining|miners]], engine room crewers, and [[farm]] laborers.<ref name="Aliens of the Galaxy" />

The servitude of the Narquois ended several [[Standard century|centuries]] later, when the authoritarian [[Galactic Empire]] was defeated in the [[Galactic Civil War]] and was replaced by a much more [[Democracy|democratic]] and egalitarian [[New Republic]]. Taking advantage of the regime change, the people of Narq sued the Neimoidians in the New Republic courts, seeking unprecedented levels of compensation for how their species had been treated in the past.<ref name="Aliens of the Galaxy" />

==Narquois in the galaxy==
[[File:Pru_Sweevant_in_da_place.png|thumb|The pirate Pru Sweevant in the castle of Maz Kanata, Takodana]]
Narquois could be found outside of their home planet, pursuing many professions throughout the galaxy.<ref name="Aliens of the Galaxy" /> Sometime after the [[Battle of Endor]], two Narquois [[Surat Nuat's gang|worked]] for [[Surat Nuat]], a [[Sullustan]] [[crime lord]] who operated on [[Akiva]]. They and four other members of Surat's gang were involved in the capture of the New Republic agent [[Jas Emari]].<ref name="Aftermath" />

About three decades later, a Narquois worked as a miner at a [[Pressy's Tumble refinery complex|refinery complex]] on the [[asteroid]] [[Pressy's Tumble]]. Due to the harsh living and working conditions on the mining colony, he and his colleagues went on a strike. However, the colony was owned by the [[First Order]], a military and [[Politics|political]] organization inspired by the principle of the defunct Galactic Empire. The Narquois miner and three other strikers were [[Death|executed]] by the [[First Order stormtrooper|stormtroopers]] of [[Captain]] [[Phasma]] for insubordination.<ref name="BTA">''[[Before the Awakening]]''</ref> Around the same time, another offworld Narquois was in the [[cantina]] of the [[1550-LEX yacht]] ''[[Serendipity]]'' on the [[Standard day|day]] that [[Han Solo]] engaged a trio of [[bounty hunter]]s—[[Hove]], [[Rigger]], and [[Strater]]—sent to capture him.<ref name="SR">''[[Smuggler's Run: A Han Solo & Chewbacca Adventure]]''</ref>

Also during the [[First Order-Resistance War|First Order–Resistance conflict]], a male Narquois named Pru Sweevant worked as a pirate, using his contacts within the [[Mining Guild]] to learn about routes taken by valuable convoys he could raid. In keeping with this species' resentment, Sweevant took particular delight in capturing Neimoidian-owned starships.<ref name="Aliens of the Galaxy" /> He was present in the [[Takodana Castle|castle]] of [[Maz Kanata]] on [[Takodana]] shortly before the First Order [[Battle of Takodana|attacked]] the premises.<ref name="Episode VII">{{Film|VII}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Narquois were created for [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']] ([[December 18]], [[2015]]), where they appeared briefly in the person of Pru Sweevant,<ref name="Episode VII" /> an alien designed by senior sculptor [[Ivan Manzella]]<ref name="Art">''[[The Art of Star Wars: The Force Awakens]]''</ref> and played by the actor [[Kiran Shah]].<ref name="Episode VII" /> However, the Narquois first appeared in [[Chuck Wendig]]'s novel [[Aftermath (novel)|''Aftermath'']] ([[September 4]], 2015),<ref name="Aftermath" /> and were first depicted in one of [[Phil Noto]]'s illustrations for [[Greg Rucka]]'s novel ''[[Smuggler's Run: A Han Solo & Chewbacca Adventure]]'' (also September 4, 2015).<ref name="SR" />

